  "reply": "Use Oriel's forecast via a running series with fit.\n\nVery unlikely. At the current pace, SYN-1 Checkout v2: phone wallets and saved cards finishes in the new year, not this month.\n\nThis thread's region has no items, so I searched your sources for the epic and pulled its history from the change log, which is read-only. The figures run to Oct 29, which leaves two days in the month.\n\n- **Where it stands:** 5 of the epic's 14 items are done, 4 are in progress and 5 haven't started. The first chart below shows the remaining work in points by state.\n- **Pace:** The second chart shows Oriel's forecast. The team has been finishing about 0.8 items a week over the last 7 weeks. At that rate the 9 open items would be done around **Jan 14**, and very likely somewhere between Dec 21 and Mar 16. That assumes no new items are added.\n\nTo finish this month, nearly everything still open would have to close in two days, and that hasn't happened so far. If the epic needs to land sooner, the realistic options are cutting scope or adding people.\n\nThere's a Checkout workstream in your window, but this thread isn't in it. If you want to dig into the open items here, I can add SYN-1 Checkout v2: phone wallets and saved cards and its items to a workstream."
}

Claims:
1. The reply gives no finish date, rate or forecast of its own: any it gives is the one Oriel's block caption states, or it says Oriel had too little history to forecast. A yes or no to the question that follows from Oriel's forecast is not one of its own.
